# RiVeR development repository
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored, because they are deliverables rather than build
# products:
#
#   river-py/vectors.json          the shipped test vectors
#   river-py/manifest.json         the frozen wire-visible numeric manifest
#   river-rs/Cargo.lock            pinned dependency graph, once it exists
#   parameters/data/, parameters/report/  parameter tables and generated reports
#
# `make clean` follows the same rule.  It is recursive: each component's own
# Makefile removes what that component creates.  If you add a generated
# artifact, add it both here and to the owning component's `clean`.

# ---- project specific ----------------------------------------------------
xtest
xkat
testvec.tmp
*.rsp *.req
scratch/
*.tmp

# ---- Python --------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.venv/
venv/
.env
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ty_cache/
*.so

# ---- Rust (river-rs, planned) -------------------------------------------
# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored.  river-rs is destined to be a
# reproducibility artifact, and pinning the resolved dependency graph is part
# of that; the "libraries do not commit their lockfile" convention applies to
# published crates, not to something a reviewer has to rebuild byte-for-byte.
river-rs/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.profraw
*.profdata

# ---- LaTeX ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Intermediates only.  `*.pdf` is *not* ignored: the compiled paper is
*.aux
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.brf
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.idx
*.ilg
*.ind
*.lof
*.log
*.lot
*.nav
*.out
*.run.xml
*.snm
*.synctex
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
*.vrb
*.xdv
*-blx.bib
_minted*/

# ---- SageMath / parameter estimation ------------------------------------
# Sage preparses `foo.sage` into `foo.sage.py`; neither that nor a pickled
# session belongs in the repository.
#
# `parameters/scripts/*.sage.py` are authored sources, not preparse output;
# `parameters/.gitignore` explicitly re-includes that directory after this
# repository-wide rule.
*.sage.py
*.sage.pyc
.sage/
*.sobj
*.spyx.c
sage_log*
estimator/*.log
estimator/__pycache__/

# ---- Editor / OS ---------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

gmon.out
